@7193. "Abraham" here = the celestial in the Human before it was made Divine; "Isaac," the spiritual, and "Jacob," the natural.

@8918[3]. "Abraham" in the highest sense represents the Lord, and in the relative sense, those in Heaven who are in the good of love and of faith in the Lord. References.

