@635. With those called "Noah," persuasions did not obstruct and absorb the Lord's operation through remains.

@1042[2]. Black in spiritual things is man's own voluntary, or evil, which absorbs and extinguishes the rays of light. @2492.

@1316[2]. The sphere of one who regards himself in everything, appropriates to itself, and, as is there said, absorbs everything that favours it, thus [it absorbs] all the delight of the Spirits around him...

@1736[2]. "He will swallow up death"...

@5217. "And they swallowed up the seven fat ears." To "swallow up" = to exterminate.

@6000[3]. Thus is the light of truth absorbed and suffocated in darkness, as the light of the sun is in what is black.

@6388[2]. Such are like objects which do not send back, but absorb the rays of light.

@8306. "The earth swallowed them" = damnation and Hell.

@HH 466. The memory with such appears darksome, being of such a nature as to absorb the rays of light and turn them into darkness.

@DLW 336. Such things conduce to absorb malignities...

@CL 510[2]. They are then swallowed up and fall down into Hell among their like.

@TCR 312[end]. In this world their bodies absorb and hide these things.

@342[end]. Used in the sense of swallowed up. @642.

@564[3]. Absorbs and suffocates the rays of light...

@569. The body absorbs them...

@SE 1393. A black colour is such that it absorbs all the rays... In like manner evil absorbs all the rays of intellectual light.

Absorb.; Insorbere.

@TCR 499[2]. Every metal etc. freely absorbs the ether...

Abstain.; Abstinere.
Abstinence.; Abstentia.

@AC 2364[end]. Effect of abstaining from evil.

