Abuse.; Abuti.
Abuse.; Abusus.

@AC 4802. There, they abuse their faculty of understanding truths to gain dominion...

@5700[2]. When they abuse heavenly order to do evil...

@6692[2]. Magic is especially the abuse of correspondences. @7026.

@7296. The abuse of Divine order. Signified.

@--[end]. The abuse of order and of correspondences. Explained. @7298, Explained. @7332[end]. @7337, Example(s). @8870[2].

@7297. The things that flow from order are not changed by abuse...

@7299. Their power of abusing order is there taken away...

@8480. The abuse of Divine good. Signified.

